        "answer": "# Newton's Second Law\n\nNewton's second law of motion describes the relationship between the net external force acting on a body and the acceleration it experiences. It states that the net external force on a body is related to the acceleration of the body .\n\nIn symbolic form for a single particle, it is given as:\n$F = \\frac{dp}{dt}$\n\nWhere:\n**F** = net external force on the particle\n**p** = momentum of the particle\n**t** = time\n\nThis law can also be extended to a system of particles, where the rate of change of the total linear momentum of the system is equal to the net external force acting on the system .\n\n**📘 Source:** NCERT Class 11 Physics • Newton Second Law"
